 ScenarioB;res;torn;ok;result
⍝ ── B — Torn board (concurrent) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝ One clerk books 500 seats while three auditors scan the board. A tear shows only
⍝ while a booking is in flight, between claiming a seat and bumping the count. At rest
⍝ the board always balances, so one PASS proves nothing. Each auditor runs in its own
⍝ thread, loops many reads, and returns its own tear count.
 NewSeats 1000
 res←⎕TSYNC ({⊢Book¨⍳⍵}&500),({+/Board¨⍵⍴0}&¨3⍴100000)
 torn←+/1↓res                       ⍝ drop the clerk's result; sum the auditors' tears
 ok←0=torn
 result←'FAIL' 'PASS'⊃⍨⎕IO+ok
 ⎕←'B torn board  : torn reads = ',⍕torn
 ⎕←'Scenario B: ',result
